content.text:
Hmm my spawnDust is convoluted with _dt handling — updateDust sets _dt each frame AFTER spawnDust is called in render order (spawnDust called after drawGroundLights; updateDust called at render start). So _dt holds previous frame dt — fine for accumulation. But the line `this._dustCd = ... || 0` is messy/nonsense. Let me simplify spawnDust to just use accumulator:

```js
spawnDust(game) {
  if (!game.player.moving || !game.world) return;
  this._dustAcc += this._dt || 0;
  if (this._dustAcc < 0.14) return;
  ...
}
```
_dustAcc initialized undefined → NaN problem: (undefined) + dt = NaN. Initialize in constructor? Simpler: `this._dustAcc = (this._dustAcc || 0) + dt`. Rewrite cleanly. Also updateDust is called before spawnDust each frame (updateDust at top, spawnDust mid) so _dt current frame set already. Order: render() calls updateWeather, updateDust(dt) (sets _dt=dt), later spawnDust uses this._dt (current frame, fine).

