content.text:
Now enemy animation improvements: quadruped run gait + attack lunge. In drawEnemy, add after scale/translate:

```js
const chase = e.state === 'chase' || e.state === 'attack';
const run = chase ? Math.sin(time * 10 + e.anim * 6) : 0;
const atk = e.attackAnim ? Math.sin(e.attackAnim * Math.PI) : 0;
// lunge toward player when striking
ctx.translate(atk * 3, -Math.abs(run) * 0.6);
```
But the bob introduced vertical bob already; combine: bob + run.

Currently: `const bob = Math.sin(time*3 + e.anim)*(...)`; `ctx.translate(0, bob)`. I'll modify: `ctx.translate(0, bob - Math.abs(run) * 0.8)` handled in one place, and insert `const run.../atk...` above switch; lunge translate after bob translate.

Legs in wolf/boar/hound/scarab/spider: modify their leg rects with run offsets.

wolf legs:
```js
p(ctx, -8, -3, 3, 4, C(dark)); p(ctx, 3, -3, 3, 4, C(dark));
```
change to use legSwing: back legs +run, front -run? For side view, legs alternate:
```js
p(ctx, -8, -3, 2, 4 + run, C(dark)); p(ctx, 3, -3, 2, 4 - run, C(dark));
```
Keep widths. Add two more legs? Simplicity: alternate front/back.

boar legs similar. hound legs. scarab 4 legs p(sx,-6,2,5) alternate ± run 0.5.

Also add attack lunge translate. Implement via edit of drawEnemy top + each case's legs.

Also player: casting sigil in renderer drawPlayerSprite. Let me do enemy edits now.

